# netsurf: element, text, comment and fragment nodes have no own properties;
# tagName / nodeName / nodeType are the prototypes' getters (patch 279)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 278)
#
# In a browser a node has no own properties: tagName is an Element.prototype
# getter, nodeName / nodeType Node.prototype's. Here every wrapper carried
# tagName, nodeName, nodeType and __ptr (never read), and once used, the
# bridge's caches -- _L / _LC / _LR (listeners, capture flags, registered
# pairs), _H (on<event> handlers), __st / __cl / __ds (style, classList,
# dataset) -- and an SVG element __vbNS; a text node an own appendChild, a
# fragment eleven own members (appendChild, removeChild, insertBefore,
# children, textContent and their __get* / __set* backends, as closures per
# fragment).
#
#  - macsurf_qjs.c: Node.prototype getters nodeType / nodeName and
#    Element.prototype tagName, read from the node (qjs_el_names: patch
#    249's casing rules, factored out of qjs_wrap_element; the strings are
#    atoms, one per tag name); DocumentFragment.prototype textContent (the
#    same this-based functions the closures used); CharacterData.prototype
#    appendChild (the no-op text nodes had). The caches and __vbNS go to the
#    object's private record (qjs_priv_get / qjs_priv_set in C,
#    __vitaP(this) in the bridge's scripts). Node.prototype's methods serve
#    fragments (they did already for everything else).
#  - vita_polyfill.js: namespaceURI / localName read __vbNS from the record;
#    element.attributes builds its Attr objects with defineProperty (Attr
#    inherits Node.prototype's getter-only nodeName / nodeType now, and the
#    strict-mode assignments threw: the first gate caught it, JS-sanitize
#    5/7).
#
# Found on the way, older than this patch: a capture listener on the event's
# target fires twice per event (dispatchEvent and click() alike).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-node-shape.html (NODESHAPE 6/6, Chromium 6/6; the
# build before fails 1-4).
